<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--What Android's own backup keeps: the Google backup, a phone-to-phone transfer, and adb backup before
Android 12. The settings, the theme, and the database: pinned entries and translation choices. Not the login, the
Anime365 token or the in-app browser's data (the site session, «Веб-плеер» logins): restored on
another phone, a login would share its refresh token with this one (BUGS #68).
A list of what to keep, not of what to leave out, so a file added later stays out until it is added
here on purpose. Android adds a database's -journal and -wal files by itself.
Since Android 12 these rules cover the Google backup and a phone-to-phone transfer only: adb backup
copies everything (FullBackup.getConfigSectionForBackupDestination has no section for it).
With targetSdk 31 or higher, Android 12+ reads android:dataExtractionRules instead: it needs the same
list.-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include
        domain="sharedpref"
        path="com.gnoemes.shikimori_preferences.xml" />
    <include
        domain="sharedpref"
        path="com.gnoemes.shikimori_themepreferences.xml" />
    <include
        domain="database"
        path="shikimori_database" />
</full-backup-content>
